{
  "slug": "claude-codex-loop",
  "name": "Claude Codex Loop",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "claude-codex-loop orchestrates a structured collaboration loop between Claude Code (designer/reviewer) and OpenAI Codex (auditor/implementer). It runs two stages — design and code — each with up to 5 rounds of iterative review plus an independent validation pass.\n\nHow it works:\n- Brainstorming (optional) — Explore requirements interactively before designing\n- Design stage — Claude Code writes a spec, Codex audits it independently each round until convergence\n- User gate — You review and approve the design before any code is written\n- Code stage — Codex implements, Claude Code reviews the full diff each round\n- Independent validation — A separate audit pass with zero prior context to catch groupthink\n\nAll work happens on a dedicated branch. Cancel anytime with /cancel-review to cleanly restore your starting state.\n\nCommands: /review-loop <task>, /cancel-review",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `autooptimize` (Autonomously optimize any project artifact (prompts, configs, code, plugins) by running end-to-end test scenarios, scoring outputs against binary…).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install claude-codex-loop@claude-community` from `Whisker17/claude-codex-loop`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
